description:
Populate SieveEnv with authentication metadata before calling the Sieve evaluator in stoa-smtp.

Files: crates/smtp/src/session.rs (or wherever sieve_delivery calls evaluate())

At the point where MessageAuthenticator results are available and before
evaluate() is called, build a SieveEnv:

```rust
let mut sieve_env = SieveEnv::new();

// Standard RFC 5183 values
sieve_env.set("domain", &config.hostname);
sieve_env.set("host", &config.hostname);
sieve_env.set("location", "MTA");
sieve_env.set("phase", "during");

// vnd.stoa.* values from authentication results
// auth_result is the output of MessageAuthenticator::verify()
match auth_result.dkim() {
    Some(r) if r.result() == DkimResult::Pass => {
        sieve_env.set("vnd.stoa.dkim-result", "pass");
        sieve_env.set("vnd.stoa.dkim-domain", r.signature().domain());
    }
    Some(_) => sieve_env.set("vnd.stoa.dkim-result", "fail"),
    None    => sieve_env.set("vnd.stoa.dkim-result", "none"),
}
match auth_result.spf() {
    Some(r) => sieve_env.set("vnd.stoa.spf-result", r.result().as_str()),
    None    => sieve_env.set("vnd.stoa.spf-result", "none"),
}
match auth_result.dmarc() {
    Some(r) => {
        sieve_env.set("vnd.stoa.dmarc-result", r.result().as_str());
        sieve_env.set("vnd.stoa.dmarc-policy", r.policy().as_str());
    }
    None => {
        sieve_env.set("vnd.stoa.dmarc-result", "none");
        sieve_env.set("vnd.stoa.dmarc-policy", "none");
    }
}
```

Then pass &sieve_env to evaluate().

Note: inspect the actual mail-auth crate API (MessageAuthenticator output types)
before implementing — adapt field names/methods to match the real API.

Defensive rules:
- If auth was not run (no MessageAuthenticator configured), all vnd.stoa.* values = "none"
- No unwrap() on auth result fields
- dkim-domain = empty string if DKIM was not present (not "none" — domain is a string, not a result)
